of books in the typical Karaite
Bible codex at the time of Yefet
by following the order in which
his commentaries were published,
based on internal evidence. It seems
that Chronicles preceded Psalms in
Ketuvim. Job preceded Proverbs.
The megillot were arranged
chronologically: Ruth, Song of
Songs, Ecclesiastes, Lamentations,
Esther. Daniel, Ezra-Nehemiah
concluded the codex. This is the
same order found in Spanish codices
of the Middle Ages. (BK)</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
